/*
 * What the OneBlock produces, per dimension.
 *
 * Copied to config/cobblemon_oneblock/oneblock.json5 on first start and never touched again,
 * so your edits always win. Delete it to get this default back. Reload with /ob reload.
 *
 * THE RULE: an island has one OneBlock in each dimension, and each draws only from its own
 * dimension's set. The Overworld anchor gives Overworld blocks, the Nether anchor gives Nether
 * blocks, the End anchor gives End blocks. Same for treasure chests.
 *
 * "weight" is relative within a dimension — higher means more common. An entry may also be a
 * bare block id, which means weight 1. Unknown blocks are logged and skipped, so listing a
 * modded block that is not installed is safe.
 *
 * TWO RULES THE SERVER ENFORCES FOR YOU, both logged when they fire:
 *  - a block that cannot stand on its own is dropped. Saplings, torches, flowers, crops, rails
 *    and anything else needing support would pop off the instant it became the anchor.
 *  - an unbreakable block is dropped. Bedrock as the anchor would soft-lock the island.
 *
 * Things worth NOT adding, learned the hard way: ice (melts into water and drains away),
 * powder snow (players fall through it into the void) and dragon eggs (teleport when hit,
 * usually off the island). Lanterns and torches look like solid blocks in a list and are not —
 * the support check catches them, but the log line is the only sign, so read it after editing.
 */
{
  // The main island. Wood, stone, ores, sand, snow — everything above and below ground.
  "overworld": [
    { "block": "minecraft:grass_block", "weight": 30 },
    { "block": "minecraft:dirt", "weight": 30 },
